        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF150  added support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/caretPositionFromPoint#shadowroots\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">options.shadowRoots</code></a> in <code class=\"notranslate\">Document.caretPositionFromPoint()</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1914596\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1914596</a> (this just flips pref <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.shadowdom.new_caretPositionFromPoint_behavior.enabled</code>)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127856674\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43563\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43563/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43563\">mdn/content#43563</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29364",
            "title": "FF150  document.caretPositionFromPoint() shadowroot options",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-30T03:36:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-30T03:35:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the one bit <code class=\"notranslate\">preload</code> that doesn't work across browsers and I wanted to know why. I added the link I found.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/preload/supported-as-values.html%3Fas%3Dtrack%26expected%3D1?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/preload/supported-as-values.html%3Fas%3Dtrack%26expected%3D1?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1886145\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1886145</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29362",
            "title": "`html.elements.link.rel.preload.as-track`: add Firefox bug URL",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-29T15:57:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-29T15:56:31.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1152698?u=5ce323090a48b425ec70128365c96809699959f7&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds partial implementation flags and notes for <code class=\"notranslate\">align-self</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">justify-self</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">place-self</code> for all browsers, when they apply to absolutely positioned elements.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tested this in Safari, Firefox, and Chrome, and discussed with Mozilla engineers <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/dshin-moz/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/dshin-moz\">@dshin-moz</a> and <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/emilio/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/emilio\">@emilio</a>.<br>\nMy understanding is that there's a missing piece in all browsers where you can't just apply the above properties and expect them to work on their own. They also require a non-auto <code class=\"notranslate\">inset</code> value.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test case: <a href=\"https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965</a></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..-9ZvzV6AW4DsEaPPX4P2XnMuJK7TIvxcku2G2RRe6HU\"><img width=\"859\" height=\"685\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..-9ZvzV6AW4DsEaPPX4P2XnMuJK7TIvxcku2G2RRe6HU\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 685px;\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The red box should be centered in the gray box.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n  .parent { position: absolute; inset: 20vmin; background: gray; }\n  .child { position: absolute; width: 50%; aspect-ratio: 1; background: red; justify-self: center; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;parent&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;child&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">style</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n  .<span class=\"pl-c1\">parent</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">position</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> absolute; <span class=\"pl-c1\">inset</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">20<span class=\"pl-smi\">vmin</span></span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">background</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> gray; }\n  .<span class=\"pl-c1\">child</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">position</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> absolute; <span class=\"pl-c1\">width</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">50<span class=\"pl-smi\">%</span></span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">aspect-ratio</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">background</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> red; <span class=\"pl-c1\">justify-self</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> center; }\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">style</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">class</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">parent</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">class</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">child</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adding <code class=\"notranslate\">inset:0;</code> on the child element makes it work.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not entirely sure I'm reading the spec correctly though, and the placement of auto-inset abspos elements may actually be correct. But, WPT seems to show browser differences in this area at least: <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Firefox bug that was filed as a result of my discussion with Mozilla engineers: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174</a></li>\n<li>Related Chromium issue: <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29342",
            "title": "Add partial implementation notes for align-self, justify-self, and place-self properties on absolute positioned elements",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-30T09:38:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-25T14:14:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "captainbrosset",
                "url": "https://github.com/captainbrosset"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update the <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn-urls</code> linter rules</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Ignore overview pages (with <code class=\"notranslate\">browser-compat</code> front matter).</li>\n<li>Prefer pages with single <code class=\"notranslate\">browser-compat</code> value.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Ensure that BCD features whose key also appears in overview pages' frontmatter, still get the reference page as <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn_url</code>.</li>\n<li>Ensure that BCD features whose key appears on multiple reference pages, get the more specific reference page as <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn_url</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29339.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4134789075\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29339\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29339/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29339\">#29339</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29341",
            "title": "fix(lint): prefer MDN pages with single browser-compat value",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T17:08:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-25T14:03:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Between versions 142 and 145, Chrome enables support for various features of the <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Local Network Access spec</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928</a> and <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically, these are:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">targetAddressSpace</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">Request</code> property, which was previously available behind a flag, and the equivalent <code class=\"notranslate\">RequestInit</code> property. AIUI, the property was finally enabled by default by version <code class=\"notranslate\">142</code>.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network-access</code> permission/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directive, which was added in 142.</li>\n<li>The more granular <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">loopback-network</code> permissions/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directives, which were added in 145.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds/updates data points as appropriate for these features.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29331",
            "title": "Chrome 142-145 support for local network access features",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T17:59:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-24T15:57:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24025?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Deno supports <code class=\"notranslate\">Error.captureStackTrace</code> since v1.22.2.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4115842329\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\">#29313</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29313.\">Fixes</span>: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4115842329\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\">#29313</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29314",
            "title": "Deno 1.23 added `Error.captureStackTrace`",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-29T12:10:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-22T12:11:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "quad",
                "url": "https://github.com/quad"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7689582?u=11ee71fc041d4f515bef665b10af491bd2d2d5ab&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With WebGPU support enabled by default in Safari 26 (shipped with macOS 26 Tahoe and iOS 26) a bunch of WebGPU features were enabled. All the features marked in this PR with <code class=\"notranslate\">\"version_added\" : \"26\"</code> were already available in previous Safari versions with the WebGPU flag enabled, and are now enabled by default.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Both <code class=\"notranslate\">core-features-and-limits</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">texture-formats-tier1</code> are enabled at least in Safari 26.2. I don't have access to a machine with 26.1 or 26.0 and I haven't found when they were added.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29309",
            "title": "Update WebGPU features for Safari",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T17:42:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-21T16:41:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ferminLR",
                "url": "https://github.com/ferminLR"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 adds support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@container\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code></a> selections where the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@container#container-query\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;container-query&gt;</code></a> part is optiona in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2016474\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2016474</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This allows you to just select a container based on its name:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"@container --name {}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">@container</span> --name {}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the subfeature. You can test this using <a href=\"https://wpt.live/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.live/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that I have set Chrome and Safari as <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> but you can tell it is coming because they pass the test on the latest versions but NOT on current versions I can access: <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html?label=master&amp;label=experimental&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html?label=master&amp;label=experimental&amp;aligned</a></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Webkit: in STP release 235 <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/17739/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-235/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/17739/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-235/</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3978053780\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43212\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43212/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43212\">mdn/content#43212</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29300",
            "title": "FF149 @container query is optional",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-31T05:25:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-20T01:24:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes standard-track exceptions.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Includes a helper script <code class=\"notranslate\">node scripts/fix-standard-track-exceptions.js</code> that allows to fix them interactively.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Follow-up of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3809800395\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28810\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28810/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28810\">#28810</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29223",
            "title": "Fix standard track exceptions",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-30T15:08:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-10T16:55:10.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 adds support for additional characters to be allowed in attribute and element names in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773312\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773312</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previously  you could only use the chars allowed in XML names - now the rules are less restrictive to allow the same chars as the HTML parser.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Spec update: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1263558481\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7991\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/7991/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7991\">whatwg/html#7991</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome states support in 143:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-143-beta#allow_more_characters_in_javascript_dom_apis\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-143-beta#allow_more_characters_in_javascript_dom_apis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6278918763708416\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6278918763708416</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Webkit added support in <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=241419\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=241419</a>  but I don't think this made it to Safari yet.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3978124831\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43218/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218\">mdn/content#43218</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29217",
            "title": "FF149 Allow more characters in DOM APIs",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-29T22:02:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-10T04:29:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 supports the <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> pseudo-element, which allows custom styling to be applied to browser search results; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We already have BCD for <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code>, however, you can combine <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> with the <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> pseudo-class to style the currently-highlighted search term on the page. This currently doesn't have any BCD, so I am using this PR to add <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm assuming it makes sense to put Chrome 144 down for this as well, as previously, there was no context in which <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> was supported. However, you might have other opinions on this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also thought about putting <code class=\"notranslate\">\"partial_implementation\": \"true\"</code> for this, but then again, <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> is fully supported in the context it is supported in. It just isn't supported in other contexts.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28882",
            "title": "Chrome 144 :current support",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-03T12:43:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-21T18:28:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is updates to add details to cover Safari support for documentId and parentDocumentId. More information on changes see the related content PR. (TBC)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28341.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3575616610\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\">#28341</a><br>\nRelated content changes in (TBC)</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28790",
            "title": "Issue-28341 webextension.api documentId and parentDocumentId updates",
